  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Offer four meaning phrases. Exactly one matches the prefix: re- is again, pre- is before, and mis- is wrong.",
      "Never put the target word itself in a choice, and never use letters, IPA, or sound clips as choices.",
      "Do not teach opaque re- words such as remember, return, report, remote, research, review, or repeat.",
      "Keep the filled pool near one third re- targets, one third pre- targets, and one third mis- targets.",
      "Tier 1 distractors are unrelated kid-world actions or things. Tiers 2 and 3 swap the other prefix meanings on the same base.",
      "Tier 3 near-misses pair reread with misread, repay with prepay, or reprint with misprint.",
      "Stems stay in kid world: school, home, food, pets, play, family, or weather. No brands. No real names; use <NAME>."
    ]
  },
